troke in the general population in addition to established risk factors</article-title><source>Eur Heart J Cardiovasc Imaging</source><volume>16</volume><issue>6</issue><year>2015</year><fpage>684</fpage><lpage>690</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">25550362</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref9"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Joshi</surname><given-names>N.V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Vesey</surname><given-names>A.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>M.C.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title><sup>18</sup>F-fluoride positron emission tomography for identification of ruptured and high-risk coronary atherosclerotic plaques: a prospective clinical trial</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>383</volume><issue>9918</issue><year>2014</year><fpage>705</fpage><lpage>713</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">24224999</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref10"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Irkle</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Vesey</surname><given-names>A.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>D.Y.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Identifying active vascular microcalcification by <sup>18</sup>F-sodium fluoride positron emission tomography</article-title><source>Nat Commun</source><volume>6</volume><year>2015</year><fpage>7495</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">26151378</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref11"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moss</surname><given-names>A.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sim</surname><given-names>A.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Adamson</surname><given-names>P.D.</given-names></nam